  "contracts": {
    "key_order": "Exact generated key comparator equals the full-field lexicographic code, retaining the generation, principal, all fingerprint bytes and server; code injectivity and strict-order/transitivity/asymmetry/trichotomy are proved without a hash injectivity assumption.",
    "ordered_maps": "Strict pairwise key order implies uniqueness. Insertion, first matching removal and head removal preserve strict order and hence unique keys.",
    "insert": "On an ordered input, actual concrete external insertion returns the full previous lookup value, writes the full supplied value and preserves every other key/value. Size grows by one exactly for an absent key and does not grow on replacement.",
    "remove": "Actual concrete external removal returns the full previous value, removes the key, never grows the map and preserves every other full value.",
    "capacity_and_victim": "Given ordered input and length at most 4096, room plus insertion preserves the bound. If an eviction victim is named, it belongs to the original map and is its minimum key under the checked comparator.",
    "key_predicates": "Erase, room and insertion preserve arbitrary predicates on stored keys, with insertion additionally requiring that predicate of its new key. These lemmas support the forthcoming generation-coherence proof."
  },
